     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Llama3: A moving average is a statistical calculation that smooths out fluctuations in data by calculating the average value of a series over a specified period, typically updated as new data becomes available.\n",
      "Mistral:  A moving average is a statistical tool that calculates the average price of a security over a specific time period, providing a simple and effective way to visualize trends and filter out short-term market noise.\n",
      "\n",
      "A moving average is often used in technical analysis for trading decisions, as it helps identify potential entry or exit points based on the relationship between prices and the moving averages. Different moving average types (such as Simple Moving Average, Exponential Moving Average, or Weighted Moving Average) may be utilized to focus on short-term or long-term trends.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from langchain_community.llms import Ollama\n",
    "llama = Ollama(model=\"llama3\")\n",
    "mistral = Ollama(model=\"mistral\")\n",
    "prompt = \"Explain what a moving average is in one sentence.\"\n",
    "print(\"Llama3:\", llama.invoke(prompt))\n",
    "print(\"Mistral:\", mistral.invoke(prompt))"
   ]
  },
